    {
      "id": "mfhhjc8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Ocean Gyres – The Circular Current System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o4f6iau",
      "content": "Gyres are large rotating systems of ocean currents formed due to the combined effect of trade winds, westerlies, and Coriolis force. Northern Hemisphere gyres rotate clockwise, while Southern Hemisphere gyres rotate anticlockwise."
    },
