    },
    {
      "id": "bqyag0q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Upwelling and Downwelling"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ujufpuw",
      "content": "• Upwelling brings nutrient-rich cold water to the surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d1df9h5",
      "content": "• Creates the world’s richest fishing grounds (Peru, Benguela)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1z95got",
      "content": "• Downwelling occurs when surface water sinks."
    },
    {
      "id": "g8evvor",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Thermohaline Circulation – Global Conveyor Belt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e17y4av",
      "content": "• Driven by density differences caused by temperature and salinity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "26qiprx",
      "content": "• Cold, saline water sinks near polar regions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cyfett3",
      "content": "• Deep currents move toward equator."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "efxz7hr",
      "content": "• Surface currents complete the cycle."
    },
    {
      "id": "6lixtbr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Climatic Importance of Ocean Currents"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Warm currents flow from equatorial regions towards higher latitudes, raising coastal temperatures and increasing precipitation.",
        "Cold currents move from polar regions to lower latitudes, often causing dry, desert-like conditions on adjacent west coasts.",
        "The Northern Indian Ocean current pattern uniquely reverses its direction seasonally due to the influence of monsoon winds."
      ],
      "id": "lcszi8s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39lg61a",
      "content": "• Gulf Stream keeps Western Europe warmer than similar latitudes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i364s1o",
      "content": "• Cold currents create coastal deserts."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kb8uw0j",
      "content": "• Currents influence cyclone formation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dunzlqw",
      "content": "• Help regulate global heat balance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j7lzn54",
      "content": "• Support marine ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "id": "d9nj52e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MASTER EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2xixlo2",
      "content": "• Warm currents move poleward; cold currents move equatorward.<br></br>• Gyres rotate clockwise in the Northern Hemisphere.<br></br>• Peru Current supports fisheries.<br></br>• Labrador Current causes dense fog.<br></br>• Indian Ocean currents reverse due to monsoon."
    }
  ],
